1. The four ceilings are CPU time (user + system), the quiet median plus a margin. Medians of
   five samples of twelve fresh processes, in six windows at load 92.9, 94.1, 75.2, 72.6, 68.7
   (and H177's load-21.4 window, which read the same CPU time):

     version          4.2-5.8 ms (quiet 4.89)   ceiling 12
     imports_nothing  7.5-10.8 ms (quiet 7.01)  ceiling 18
     inspect_ops     39.2-45.0 ms (quiet 37.97) ceiling 95
     imports_all     40.0-42.5 ms (quiet 36.19) ceiling 90

   The wall-clock ceilings were 40/45/100/90 ms; at load 106-130 `--version`, which compiles
   nothing, read 13.0 ms and `imports_all` went red at 92.8/101.4 ms. The load average is still
   printed beside the numbers as provenance, and no "red under load is not a regression" reading
   remains. A crossed CPU ceiling is a regression.

2. declaration.cost keeps the per-declaration ceiling (60 us, the number unchanged, read in CPU:
   27.5-28.5 us in every window at load 68-94), gains the absolute total the ruling chose
   (12 ms: H177 5.3's candidate, quiet total plus the 4.6 ms regression it was meant to name),
   and asserts on every round that each (phase, module) among parse, GCT and declare appears
   exactly once (H177 5.3's candidate 3). The 30% share is deleted, not commented out.

   The phase report had no CPU field, and the wall reading of those same phases was 75-104 us
   per declaration at load 106-112 against 27.5-28.5 us of CPU (same-window wall/cpu 1.57 at
   load 94). Commit 46e837240 is that instrument: `cpu_ns` beside `wall_ns`
   (CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID / GetProcessTimes, -1 where neither exists), and the line reports
   an error on such a platform instead of falling back to the wall clock.

3. The refusal now reads "invalid tiles plan: cublas_bf16 needs reassociate, change_precision,
   finite_math on the matmul node and is missing change_precision"; a cublas_bf16 stage that is
   not a matmul node says that. Red before: with the guard and the old message, feat.modules.tiles
   plan_validation FAILED (stderr "invalid tiles plan: mixed GEMM permissions"). Green after:
   plan_validation PASS. One producer only (modules/tiles/src/schedule.cpp), nothing else pinned
   the message, no new diagnostic code -- 0x0001D5 stays deleted.

4. Gate on the final commit fc0dceecf: the whole fast layer
   (`-Plan smoke,test/plans/feat -Tier fast -Jobs 8`, 5715 tests) plus the changed slow plan
   test/plans/perf/startup.plan.toml in full -- total 5715, pass 5701, fail 0, skip 14;
